WEBVTT

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:04.470
Ask Airbnb.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:13.040
Years ago I led design on a zero-to-one
initiative. Airbnb Transportation.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:26.400
I worked on flight integration on Search.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:36.100
On-trip needs like airport lounges,
baggage storage, and public transit.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:48.890
And tools to help build your trip.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:58.420
Sadly, COVID killed these projects.
But I learnt one valuable lesson.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.110
Planning is hard.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:18.140
While Airbnb is good at booking stays, we
have strong competitors, like Booking,

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:28.970
VRBO, and Expedia.

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:38.280
Users also rely on search and
AI to figure out where to go.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:57.600
Tickets are bought on Google
Flights or Skyscanner.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.380
With various transportation
apps to get places.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.900
While everything is planned
on Calendar and Maps.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:37.240
What if you could just ask Airbnb?

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:45.240
I've been reimagining Airbnb with AI.

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:55.860
Three things make a trip. Where.
When. And who's coming?

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:08.480
Or you can just ask, and
the globe responds.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.870
Like — spin.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.900
Or dance.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:30.360
Or simple yes or no questions
like — are you human?

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:48.870
Or AI?

00:03:54.780 --> 00:04:02.780
Then ask it anything you want. Like, take
me somewhere that feels like Star Wars.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:24.440
And it thinks, gathers and gives answers.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:34.240
You can walk the snowy mountains where
they filmed the Battle of Hoth.

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:53.740
Find the hidden rebel bases in Guatemala.

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:08.940
Or fly to the deserts of
Tatooine in Tunisia.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:38.000
And ask more questions — like
“how do I get there?”

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:58.920
And it finds the nearest airport,
and gives directions.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:08.640
And you can ask “show me flights.”

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:24.380
And it delivers flight options
during popular times.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:46.340
You can also ask it to build a roadtrip,
like to New York, and it thinks,

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:59.000
then builds the route —

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:08.540
SF to Reno, Salt Lake, Moab, all the way
to NY, with driving times in between.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:21.580
Or maybe you're thinking
something different.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:28.060
Like — a more scenic route.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:45.820
And it re-routes to fit your ask.

00:07:47.760 --> 00:07:53.260
Let's ask something more specific like —

00:07:59.320 --> 00:08:06.820
my daughter wants to see giraffes
in the wild next summer.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:16.480
And it auto fills your dates
and guests, and searches.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:27.320
Do you want self-drive safaris
in South Africa?

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:37.560
Natural watering holes in Namibia?

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:46.340
Or stay in kid-friendly
lodges in Masai Mara.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:56.420
Then I can dive into the city.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:06.200
I can heart homes I like, and it'll
start collecting my preferences.

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:21.340
And I can browse and heart experiences
I'm interested in.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:31.810
Choose some flight options for the family.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:39.310
And book airport pick-ups or car rentals.

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:46.700
Then I tap “plan,” and it
auto creates my trip.

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:58.520
If you like what you see,
you can just “book.”

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:15.770
Then it automatically gets
added as an upcoming trip.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:25.690
You can tap to see where you've gone.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:31.220
And if I tap a future trip.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:41.000
Your itinerary is already built for you.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:50.940
And you can see all your plans
on a day-to-day schedule.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:11:02.040
You can sync to your own Google Calendar.

00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:21.170
So everything you need is in one place.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:32.740
And at any point, add anything
extra you might need.

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:49.020
You dream, AI does the rest.
